  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Kurapati Srinivas vs The State Of Telangana on 24 July, 2025 Author: N.Tukaramji Bench: N.Tukaramji The Honourable Sri Justice N.Tukaramji Criminal Petition No. 9252 Of 2025 Order",
    "facts": "This Criminal Petition is filed under Section 528 of Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 (for short 'BNSS, 2023') seeking quashment of the proceedings in FIR No.362 of 2025 on the file of Jangaon, against the petitioner/accused. 2. The petitioner is arrayed as accused in FIR No.362 of 2025 registered for the offences punishable under Sections 272, 275 of BNS. Accordingly, the complainant and his staff apprehended the petitioner and seized Kurapati Srinivas vs The State Of Telangana on 24 July, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/162362070/",
    "arguments": "The prosecution case in brief is that the petitioner/accused is involved in selling and purchasing the banned Tobacco products and the Police concerned has seized the said Tobacco products worth of Rs.9,150/- from the possession of the petitioner. 5. Learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that a Coordinate Bench of this Court vide Criminal Petition Nos.3731 and Batch on considering similar allegations and the merits [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the petitioner therein. He further submits that the police have registered the present crime in violation of the orders passed by this 2 NTR,J Court. Hence, prayed for quashment of the proceedings against the petitioner. 6. Learned Additional Public Prosecutor would submit that the petitioner has been found with the Tobacco products and investigation is pending. However fairly admitted that in the authority cited by the petitioner in the similar circumstances, the proceedings against the petitioner therein were [LEAKAGE_MASK]. 10. Having regard to similar factual position, a Coordinate Bench of this Court in Crl.P.No.6235 of 2022 held that against the allegations of illegal sale and transportation of tobacco products the accusations under Sections 188, 269, 270, 272, 273, 278, 328 read with Sections 511, 336, 409 and 420 of I.P.C., cannot be maintained and [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the petitioners therein.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The prosecution case in brief is that the petitioner/accused is involved in selling and purchasing the banned Tobacco products and the Police concerned has seized the said Tobacco products worth of Rs.9,150/- from the possession of the petitioner. 5. Learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that a Coordinate Bench of this Court vide Criminal Petition Nos.3731 and Batch on considering similar allegations and the merits [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the petitioner therein.",
    "respondent_arguments": "He further submits that the police have registered the present crime in violation of the orders passed by this 2 NTR,J Court. Hence, prayed for quashment of the proceedings against the petitioner. 6. Learned Additional Public Prosecutor would submit that the petitioner has been found with the Tobacco products and investigation is pending. However fairly admitted that in the authority cited by the petitioner in the similar circumstances, the proceedings against the petitioner therein were [LEAKAGE_MASK].",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "10. Having regard to similar factual position, a Coordinate Bench of this Court in Crl.P.No.6235 of 2022 held that against the allegations of illegal sale and transportation of tobacco products the accusations under Sections 188, 269, 270, 272, 273, 278, 328 read with Sections 511, 336, 409 and 420 of I.P.C., cannot be maintained and [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the petitioners therein."
  },
